WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.410
Speaker 1: We have sadly tragic news from
Ukraine, where an American journalist has

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:11.929
been killed by Russian forces and another
journalist has been shot.

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:16.059
There were there were some incorrect things
reported about this story, and we're going

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:17.310
to correct those.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:23.400
The Jerusalem Post reporting American journalists
killed another wounded by Russian forces near

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.900
Kiev.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:31.600
The slain journalist was identified by Ukrainian
police as a 51 year old U.S. citizen and media

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.170
correspondent.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:39.739
An American journalist was killed and another
wounded by Russian forces in Heirpod, near

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:42.360
the Ukrainian capital of Kiev.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:49.699
The killed journalist was identified by Ukrainian
police as Bret Renard, a 51 year old journalist,

00:00:49.699 --> 00:00:52.320
filmmaker and U.S. citizen.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:58.690
While the Ukrainian authorities initially
identified Renard as the New York Times correspondent,

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.670
he was not in Ukraine on behalf of the Times.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.290
So that's an important detail in the New York
Times also putting this out.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:10.670
This doesn't make it any less tragic, but
initially it was reported as a journalist

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.659
working for the New York Times in Ukraine
was shot and killed.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:17.509
It happens not to be true.

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:20.870
The New York Times putting out a statement
saying We are deeply saddened to hear of Bret

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:22.090
Raynaud's death.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:26.840
Brant was a talented filmmaker who had contributed
to the New York Times over the years.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.159
Though he had contributed to the Times in
the past, most recently 2015, he was not on

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:34.810
assignment for any desk at the Times in Ukraine.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.829
Early reports that he worked for time circulated
because he was wearing a time's press badge

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:42.180
that he had been issued for an assignment
many years ago.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.579
That's actually really common.

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:49.290
I know many, many journalists and reporters
who will just use an old press pass.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.000
I've done it as well.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.860
A decade ago.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:59.369
Sometimes it's just hard to get a new press
pass and you just use an old one.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:00.369
And that's it.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:03.789
You're just identified as press and that that's
basically it.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:10.560
So extremely, extremely tragic story, and
it is getting very, very serious there, including

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.000
not only do we now have journalists who have
been killed, but there is also video which

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.300
we're not going to play because it's still
very it's still very unclear exactly what

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.880
is allowed in terms of footage on YouTube
as well as on Instagram and Facebook, and

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.140
a lot of the platforms were on.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:35.170
But there is now footage of from Mariupol
of what appears to be and it has not been.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.350
It has not been contested at this point.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:43.580
Russian tanks just firing upon a civilian
apartment building.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:48.170
Now will the Russians later say, Well, we
believed it to be a base of operations for,

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.360
I don't know.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.610
They've not said it yet.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.740
And the video has not been contested.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.790
So this is all getting very ugly.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:59.240
And in the midst of this, we have conflicting
reports.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:05.280
On the one hand, there are reports that progress
has been made on a potential serious cease

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.110
fire and peace talks between Ukraine and Russia.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.810
That's good news if it's true.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:16.670
At the same time, there are reports being
widely publicized that Vladimir Putin is now

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.060
looking to escalate the war.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:23.150
Seeking military equipment from China could
both be true.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.080
Sure, it continues to move very quickly.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:32.890
And by the by Wednesday or Thursday, we should
have a sense as to whether the reports of

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:38.440
the cease fire talks getting closer is accurate
because typically those don't take more than

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.620
a few days from what a number of different
experts are saying.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.800
We will follow it.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.941
Let me know on Twitter at David Pakman what
you expect for the week ahead.

